WEBVTT

00:00:08.760 --> 00:00:15.070
Thomas Flintridge III presents The Squawkers, a variation in pop music.

00:00:15.960 --> 00:00:19.160
Old Flintridge may be eccentric, but he's a real swinger.

00:00:19.460 --> 00:00:22.340
I gotta see Jameson's reaction to this private preview.

00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:35.600
Groovy, man. Groovy. Right, Jameson?

00:00:35.830 --> 00:00:37.290
Great, great.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.940
A swinger? Jameson is not.

00:00:40.450 --> 00:00:42.410
I wouldn't have missed this for anything.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:55.930
What's going on here?

00:00:56.270 --> 00:00:57.710
I thought it was part of the show.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:00:59.960
That was no ordinary Sonic Black.

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.920
It was aimed. And here comes another one.

00:01:08.250 --> 00:01:11.580
Cyrus Flintridge is only the beginning.

00:01:17.260 --> 00:01:19.800
Taking off those instruments one by one was no coincidence.

00:01:20.750 --> 00:01:23.770
Flintridge and his music muddlers were somebody's target for the night.

00:01:24.290 --> 00:01:25.590
I'd like to know who.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.160
Old spider sense tells me I'm getting warm.

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:35.340
So, Spider-Man thinks to find the source of my sonic beam.

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:36.630
Heh heh heh.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:39.850
Well, I'll give him a clue.

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:42.450
Here we go again.

00:01:47.710 --> 00:01:48.850
Child adversary.

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:52.240
Now I play for real.

00:01:53.200 --> 00:01:54.520
Here comes a whopper.

00:01:55.540 --> 00:01:57.620
Heh heh heh heh heh.

00:01:58.340 --> 00:01:59.970
That should take care of...

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.490
I'm positive it came from here.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.990
Empty, not a scrap of paper.

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:14.150
Beethoven's Fifth?

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:16.790
From bop to Beethoven.

00:02:17.010 --> 00:02:18.150
There's got to be a connection.

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:28.680
...for this abominable rock and roll boom.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.670
If his money can buy the ears of the public, then I shall even the fight.

00:02:36.470 --> 00:02:40.910
He will pay me dearly, and I will build a conservatory

00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:45.550
and restore the true beauty of classical music to the world.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:48.300
And should he refuse...

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:57.060
I tell you, Jameson, this fiend has gone too far.

00:02:57.560 --> 00:02:59.980
Not only does he admit causing the sonic blast...

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:01.740
Now he's blackmailing me.

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:05.190
He wants me to leave $100,000 in a violin case

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:06.610
at the foot of Beethoven's statue.

00:03:07.750 --> 00:03:10.830
If you call the police, I will dispose of them as easily

00:03:10.830 --> 00:03:14.190
as I disposed of your so-called instruments last night.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:19.340
I refuse to pay one penny to that sonic swindler.

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:21.310
Don't get so steamed up, Flintridge.

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.220
I think I know a way to trap him.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:24.920
Miss Brandt!

00:03:25.190 --> 00:03:26.050
Yes, Mr. Jameson?

00:03:26.210 --> 00:03:27.490
Get Parker on the phone.

00:03:27.820 --> 00:03:29.060
I have a job for him.

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:39.900
Central Park tonight at Beethoven's statue. Will do, Mr. Jameson. So, old JJ wants Peter Parker to

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:45.970
spring the trap. I have a feeling that before the night is over, it'll be a job for Spider-Man.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:59.080
Concert's over. Maybe now we'll see some action. Let go my spider senses. This must be it. Watch this!

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:05.340
Violin case, gone.

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:09.300
When that blockbustin' blackmailer finds out the case is empty,

00:04:09.740 --> 00:04:13.020
he'll be after Flintridge, and Spider-Man better get there first.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:18.930
Seems okay.

00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:23.240
My spider senses are signaling danger.

00:04:23.670 --> 00:04:28.910
This time I will play a concerto that double-crossing Flintridge will never forget.

00:04:30.190 --> 00:04:31.670
Feel it. A sonic wave.

00:04:32.750 --> 00:04:36.560
My high-five.

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:38.940
No. No, stop.

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:41.040
My red horn. Stop.

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:44.830
He can't have gone far.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:47.590
I'll bet my webs he comes out into that alley.

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:52.710
Right on cue. Feel it.

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:58.500
Unless he can fly, I've got him trapped.

00:05:29.210 --> 00:05:29.970
Still on the.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:31.200
and after Flintridge.

00:05:31.420 --> 00:05:34.080
I've got a feeling there's more to this than blackmail.

00:05:35.110 --> 00:05:37.570
My priceless collection of modern music,

00:05:37.790 --> 00:05:39.910
destroyed, deliberately demolished.

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:41.530
Terrible, terrible!

00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:43.710
But at least he didn't get the money.

00:05:43.970 --> 00:05:44.530
That's right.

00:05:44.670 --> 00:05:47.910
So now he's upped his demands to $500,000

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:50.370
so he can build a conservatory of his own.

00:05:50.990 --> 00:05:53.000
Did you say five?

00:05:53.420 --> 00:05:57.040
If I don't bring it in person to my conservatory tonight,

00:05:57.380 --> 00:05:59.380
he threatens to reduce it to rubble.

00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:05.750
Jameson what do I do now? Let's not panic Parker will be here shortly with the pictures of the culprit

00:06:05.750 --> 00:06:13.620
You got the pictures? Well, yes, and no why can't you teenagers ever give a straight answer?

00:06:14.030 --> 00:06:17.310
Did you get a picture of the blackmailer?

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:23.560
Yes, but what the fiddler blasted the camera right out of my hand

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:29.750
That's right. Mr. Flintridge a fiddler with a deadly sonic violin and

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:30.820
He's after you.

00:06:31.190 --> 00:06:33.070
What am I going to do, JJ?

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:38.090
If I were you, I'd be at the conservatory tonight with the money.

00:06:38.990 --> 00:06:39.830
Thanks, JJ.

00:06:40.050 --> 00:06:41.870
That's just what I'd hoped you'd say.

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:52.860
Who's there?

00:06:55.540 --> 00:06:58.040
Just your friendly neighborhood Spider-Man.

00:06:59.360 --> 00:06:59.960
You're...

00:07:00.680 --> 00:07:06.120
Hand me the satchel, Flintridge, and then get lost or you may wind up playing a harp.

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:12.310
Jameson was right. You are a crook. Well, you won't get away with this.

00:07:20.270 --> 00:07:27.000
The satchel inside, as I instructed. If he drink me again, I'll keep my promise.

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:29.450
Flintridge is bound to go for the police.

00:07:30.090 --> 00:07:32.770
If I can just stall that vindictive virtuoso,

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:36.320
something tells me it's time to face the music.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:46.140
Hold it, Fiddler. There's a string attached.

00:07:56.330 --> 00:07:59.560
For your web, Spider-Man. Give me some money.

00:08:00.160 --> 00:08:01.460
Come and get it, maestro.

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:09.590
It's...

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:17.040
Why don't you go a little faster, officer?

00:08:17.610 --> 00:08:19.850
Not without a pilot's license, Mr. Flintridge.

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:22.010
Why don't you give up and save yourself?

00:08:22.880 --> 00:08:24.620
I can't hear you, fiddler.

00:08:24.890 --> 00:08:26.050
Over those sirens.

00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:28.580
You can't do this to me.

00:08:28.930 --> 00:08:29.930
Let me go.

00:08:30.920 --> 00:08:33.620
It seems to me I've heard that song before.

00:08:37.540 --> 00:08:38.720
Where's Spider-Man?

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:39.900
He's been here.

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:41.240
There's his calling card.

00:08:41.840 --> 00:08:48.340
The villainous violinist captured by your friendly neighborhood Spider-Man.

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:51.360
By George, that Parker boy was right.

00:08:51.580 --> 00:08:52.680
He is a fiddler.

00:08:52.910 --> 00:08:53.790
Name's Otto.

00:08:54.280 --> 00:08:56.300
Used to play second fiddle with the symphony orchestra.

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:59.350
How would you know about good music?

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:02.430
you and your rock and roll rabble.

00:09:02.930 --> 00:09:07.220
My dear fellow, I also sponsor the symphony orchestra.

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:09.980
Put this on the record player, Ms. Brandt.

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:11.700
It's a present from Flintridge,

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:14.150
called Symphony for a Summer Night.

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:17.510
That's my kind of music.

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:26.310
It does, Mr. Jameson,

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:28.510
but you didn't read the small print.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:29.630
It says,

00:09:30.220 --> 00:09:33.440
A sonic symphony for the world of tomorrow.

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:34.530
No!

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:09.370
just like flies look out here comes the spider-man is he strong listen bud he's got radio active

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:17.190
blood can you swing from a thread take a look overhead hey there there goes the spider-man

00:10:17.730 --> 00:10:27.570
the chill of night the scene of a crime like the street of light he arrives just in time

00:10:27.570 --> 00:10:29.970
Spider-Man, Spider-Man

00:10:31.280 --> 00:10:34.530
He's ignored.

00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:37.760
Action is his reward to him.

00:10:38.210 --> 00:10:40.210
Life is a great big bang up.

00:10:40.710 --> 00:10:44.290
Wherever there's a hang up, you'll find a Spider-Man.
